This README is superseded by the PDF manual and this includes all changes for
version v2.03.14 that runs under Windows, *nix, Linux etc with the GnuCOBOL
compiler v2 and v3. It is recommended to always use the latest release, which is
currently v3.2 Final (as of 1 Nov 2026).

cobxref for Micros :

This version supports both fixed, variable and free format Cobol source files
creating Cobol cross references listings.

It also supports user supplied names for data, section, paragraph,
program and modules to 63 characters IF using the latest GnuCobol code base v3.

It has been tested against production sources - well in excess of
1000 programs as well as various test source programs as well as large sources
exceeding 64,000 source lines.

I have not tested it with Windows.

[ There are some bugs :

1. Around using CALL verbs in that they also appear in the
un-referenced sections of any program listing very near the bottom.
Simple way to fix this is to do a dummy call for each one affected at the bottom
of your program which is NOT called or executed. ]

2. Occasional errors around missing variables that are present as confirmed by
being referenced else where.

3. Odd behaviour regarding CDF copy replacing where there is a large list of
such replacing statements. This is a bug in the supplemental module printcbl.
This is the last nested module in the source file.
This bug also applies to the standalone version of the same program stored
within the GnuCobol contrib folder.

I will try and find time to locate and fix it but at the moment very busy
working on ACAS development for Payroll for the US market.
This is more to keep me occupied than anything else :)

Read the Changelog for latest updates and bug fixes.

This project area (cobxref) also has the current version for
IBM MVS Ansi Cobol at:
https://sourceforge.net/projects/cobxref/files/MVS3.8J-cobxref.rar/download

It does not provide support for COPY libraries due to no demand.
In any event, such would require adding a extra support module into MVS to
allow Cobol programs access to the PDS file system. See the docs for more info.
This module has been tested.

Please report all bugs found for the GnuCOBOL version to the GNUCobol contrib
forum at https://sourceforge.net/p/gnucobol/discussion/contrib/ and send a
copy to the author at vbcoen@gmail.com if urgent or a show stopper.

Bugs for the IBM version direct to author at vbcoen@gmail.com with a subject
of MVS bug.



Vincent B. Coen
Last update 1 November 2026.

